  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.16.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.16.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "According to a second meaning, we have the investigation of matters in the special in rhetoric; and in this sense the Sophists say that a hypothesis must be proposed.",
    "chunk_index": 37,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.16.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.16.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And, according to a third signification, the beginning of a proof is called a hypothesis, as being the begging of certain matters with a view to the establishment of another in question.",
    "chunk_index": 38,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.16.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.16.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Thus it is said that Democritus used a hypothesis, namely, that of atoms and a vacuum; and Asclepiades that of atoms and pores.",
    "chunk_index": 39,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.16.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.16.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Now, when applied to mathematics, the term hypothesis is to be taken in the third sense.",
    "chunk_index": 40,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.17",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.17",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "That Pythagoras was not the only one who duly honoured arithmetic, but that his best known disciples did so too, being wont to say that “all things fit number.”",
    "chunk_index": 41,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.18",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.18",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "That arithmetic has as its immediate end chiefly the theory of science, than which there is no end either greater or nobler. And its second end is to bring together in one all that is found in determinate substance.",
    "chunk_index": 42,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.19",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.19",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Who among the mathematicians has made any discovery?",
    "chunk_index": 43,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.20.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.20.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Eudemus relates in his Astrologies that Œnopides found out the circle of the zodiac and the cycle of the great year.",
    "chunk_index": 44,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.20.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.20.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And Thales discovered the eclipse of the sun and its period in the tropics in its constant inequality.",
    "chunk_index": 45,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.20.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.20.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And Anaximander discovered that the earth is poised in space, and moves round the axis of the universe.",
    "chunk_index": 46,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic#Anat.Arith.20.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/anatolius-arithmetic",
    "canonical_ref": "Anat.Arith.20.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And Anaximenes discovered that the moon has her light from the sun, and found out also the way in which she suffers eclipse. And the rest of the mathematicians have also made additions to these discoveries.",
    "chunk_index": 47,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 275,
    "date_range": [
      265,
      283
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
